messages:
Taylor (sales): Morning team — FinCloud POC kickoff tomorrow 11am PT. Scope: streaming SDK (Node + Python), function/tool calling, and strict structured JSON outputs. Their infosec sent a questionnaire and they also want a Dedicated capacity price ballpark. Any immediate blockers?

Maya (solutions-eng): Which SDKs are primary? Do they require VPC peering or on-prem? Also: do they expect model pinning and canary rollouts?

Taylor (sales): Primary devs are Node + Python. They require VPC peering + customer KMS for keys on Private. Yes to canary; want fallback to smaller model if latency spikes. Questionnaire attached in the thread (see PDF link they sent).

Jordan (presales-engineer): I can cover the streaming + function-calling demo. Quick Node streaming example for our SDK (very terse):

```js
// streaming + function call example (Node)
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
const stream = client.chat.stream({
  model: 'rwd-llama-13b',
  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Schedule meeting and return JSON' }],
  tools: [
    { name: 'calendar.create', description: 'Create calendar events', parameters: { type: 'object' } }
  ],
  structured_output: { type: 'json', schema: { event: { title: 'string', time: 'string' } } }
});

stream.on('event', (e) => {
  if (e.type === 'function_call') console.log('invoke tool', e.tool);
  if (e.type === 'token') process.stdout.write(e.delta);
  if (e.type === 'structured_output') console.log('parsed JSON', e.json);
});

stream.start();
```

Jordan (presales-engineer): Notes: 1) For function/tool calling over streaming, listen for 'function_call' events and then respond with tool outputs via the same stream. 2) We can set a strict JSON schema in structured_output to get validated outputs server-side; we also provide a client-side helper to coerce/validate.

Maya (solutions-eng): On security: we can provide SOC2 report, pen test summary, and our standard Private deployment KMS integration checklist. For hosted flows we redact/store minimal retention by default — I'll attach the standard security pack and a short FAQ for the questionnaire.

Alex (infra): For Dedicated pricing: rough committed estimate for an enterprise-grade baseline (8 x A100-class GPUs) is typically in the ~"$40k–$85k/month" range depending on model/throughput and networking. Host/usage (hosted API) per-token pricing remains lower friction but less isolated. I can produce a precise quote if you share target RPS, avg seq length, and 95p latency SLO.

Taylor (sales): Perfect. They asked about a canary strategy that falls back to smaller model if latency > 200ms P95 for 2 consecutive minutes. Is that supported?

Maya (solutions-eng): Yes — our routing policies support latency-based fallback with a configurable window. We can template a rollout policy for them.

Jordan (presales-engineer): I'll spin up a minimal demo repo with Node + Python examples (streaming + function calls + structured output) and a tiny test harness simulating their latency conditions. Will include README with the exact API calls and a small recorded session.

Jordan (presales-engineer): Demo plan timeline:
- within 24h: demo repo + sandbox token (rate-limited)
- within 48h: recorded streaming demo + example canary config

Maya (solutions-eng): I'll start answering the checklist questions: data residency, retention windows, encryption-at-rest/in-transit, KMS flow, SOC2 link, and a contact for an audit call.

Taylor (sales): Action items:
- Jordan: demo repo + sandbox token + sample canary config (24–48h)
- Alex: draft Dedicated commit pricing deck + ask for RPS/seq lengths
- Maya: attach security pack + start the questionnaire answers
- Taylor: schedule kickoff call and capture PoC success criteria from FinCloud

Taylor (sales): Thanks — please @mention me when the repo/token are live. I'll loop in FinCloud and share the questionnaire now. :thumbsup:

sec-bot: Uploaded security_pack_v1.pdf to the thread.

Alex (infra): FYI — if they want on-prem air-gapped, that adds ~2–4 weeks to delivery for packaging and onsite validation.

Taylor (sales): Noted. I'll confirm with their infra lead.

Maya (solutions-eng): I'll be available for the infosec call if they want a technical deep-dive.

Jordan (presales-engineer): Ping me if they want a live demo during the kickoff — I can share screen and walk through streaming events and function invocation.

Taylor (sales): Great. Closing this thread for now — will reopen with demo link. :white_check_mark:
